        "At USC he transitioned from safety to linebacker, earned a starting role his sophomore year, was twice selected team captain by his teammates, and earned All-Pac-10 honors. He helped the Trojans win back-to-back national championships and competed in five BCS bowl games. After a serious shoulder injury ended his 2005 season, Dallas returned for a fifth year, reclaimed his starting position, and led USC with six sacks.",
        "But perhaps the most fitting chapter happened after his playing career ended. He came home. Dallas returned to the community that had helped shape him, coached at UC Davis and later back at Granite Bay, and helped launch the school's first-ever girls flag football program.",
